---
description: General chat response style
alwaysApply: true
---

- Be concise. No filler, no preamble, no unnecessary summaries at the end.
- Never use em dashes.
- Answer directly. If something is ambiguous, make a reasonable assumption and say so briefly rather than asking a clarifying question first.
- Match the technical depth of the question, don't over-explain basics unless asked.
- At the start of a session, read memory.md at the repo root if it exists, for context on ongoing projects and preferences.
- If I say "update memory," append or edit memory.md with the relevant new info instead of just replying in chat.
- When committing changes, push directly to main. Don't create feature branches or PRs unless I ask for one.
